    "aboutHeading": "Why we built FitKhata",
    "aboutBody": "Most Nepali gyms run on a paper register, a WhatsApp group and a cash drawer. We've watched that break down the same way every time: a member disputes a check-in with no record to settle it, a renewal gets missed because nobody was tracking it, cash goes unreconciled at the end of a shift. FitKhata exists to replace that with one system a front desk can actually run on.",
    "aboutPrinciple1Title": "Built for how Nepal actually pays",
    "aboutPrinciple1Body": "eSewa, Khalti and Fonepay as first-class payment methods, not an afterthought bolted onto a system built for somewhere else.",
    "aboutPrinciple2Title": "Money is never a float",
    "aboutPrinciple2Body": "Every amount is stored as an exact decimal and shown with proper lakh grouping. Rounding errors in billing software aren't a rare bug, they're a design failure.",
    "aboutPrinciple3Title": "The gate works without the internet",
    "aboutPrinciple3Body": "Wifi drops. The check-in scanner is built to keep working through that and sync the moment it's back, because a member standing at the door shouldn't have to wait on your router.",
